{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1451357-spirit-combat","id":1451357,"title":"Spirit combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-08T10:52:35-07:00","id":1451357,"title":"Spirit combat","content":"Hi, a pretty dumb question, but I can't find it.<br /> <br /> If you would hit a manifested spirit with a sword or a gun in the 1st edition of the CoD, what type of damage would you do? Bashing or lethal?<br /> <br /> I know all ephemeral being receive bashing damage in the 2nd edition, but the 1st edition is different. Ghost can't be hit at all by regular weapons in the 1st edition for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T11:43:03-07:00","id":1451363,"title":"","content":"I believe this is how it goes:<br /> <br /> Ghosts can't be struck by normal weapons in first edition because they don't normally materialize; &quot;manifestation&quot; in first edition describes a state more like second edition's &quot;Open&quot; Influence Condition, where the ghost's Twilight presence is close enough to project visible signs of its influence and it becomes able to exert its powers on the material world, but the ghost remains ephemeral.<br /> <br /> Spirits using the Materialize Numen incorporate physically and can thus be struck normally, doing the damage the attack would normally do. Characters who travel into the Shadow Realm by whatever means enter the same spiritual state of matter as spirits there, and thus can strike spirits found there normally as well. As for spirits in Twilight, first edition's &quot;blessed and enchanted items&quot; damage them the same way they damage ghosts, and their spirit bans apply regardless of whether the subject of the ban is in Twilight or not.<br /> <br /> The second edition rule on bashing damage to spirits appears to represent spirits lacking any vital organs to suffer damage, regardless of whether they are in the Shadow Realm, Twilight, or materialized. First edition doesn't bother with this distinction, and is just concerned with whether or not the spirit can be struck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T14:22:34-07:00","id":1451385,"title":"","content":"Hey man, thanks. I completely read over that. Now I understand.<br /> <br /> Manifest is not Materialized. And the Open Condition does use the word manifest if you use that on a location. It all makes sense now. <br /> <br /> Also the 2nd edition assumes they don't have internal organs and doesn't make a distinction between ghosts, spirits and angels. Interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1873,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","user":"Jan Paparazzi","date":". 06-08-2021, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2